## Purpose

Refs #38175.

Add `SupportsEncoderCudaGraph` integration for `LlavaOnevisionForConditionalGeneration`, covering both image and video inputs.

The implementation:

- captures the LLaVA-OneVision vision tower + multimodal projector as the fixed-shape CUDA graph region;
- keeps any-resolution image merge/unpadding and video pooling/newline assembly outside the graph;
- separates raw ViT token budgets from final LLM multimodal token counts;
- supports image and video item sizing, selection, replay buffers, eager fallback, and output post-processing;
- uses a capture axis for the number of padded vision tiles, so a large token-budget bucket does not force every request to replay the maximum tile count;
- updates the encoder CUDA graph compatibility matrix and adds LLaVA-OneVision to the existing image/video E2E CUDA graph test.

